# Trivy ignore list.
#
# Entries here MUST carry a justification and an expiry date. An indefinite
# suppression is indistinguishable from an unnoticed vulnerability.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pip's vendored dependency manifest
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both of these are read by Trivy from a single file:
#   /usr/local/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt
# which declares  msgpack==1.1.2  and  setuptools==70.3.0.
#
# Neither is reachable from application code:
#   * setuptools 70.3.0 is a manifest entry only -- the importable setuptools
#     in the image is 84.0.0, above both fixed versions (78.1.1 / 83.0.0).
#   * msgpack 1.1.2 is genuinely vendored under pip/_vendor/msgpack, but it is
#     used solely by pip's HTTP cache during package resolution. pip does not
#     run in the container at runtime; the app imports neither package.
#
# The real fix is a multi-stage build that keeps pip out of the runtime image (#160)
# entirely -- see the linked issue. These suppressions exist only until then,
# and expire so they cannot quietly become permanent.
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-11-30
CVE-2026-59890 exp:2026-11-30
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-11-30
